# Dayflow — Human Resource Management System

> **Every workday, perfectly aligned.**

Dayflow is a full-stack Human Resource Management System designed to digitize and streamline core HR operations such as employee onboarding, profile management, attendance tracking, leave management, payroll visibility, approval workflows, notifications, and analytics.

The system provides separate access and functionality for **Admin/HR Officers** and **Employees**.

---

## 📌 Project Overview

Dayflow provides a centralized platform where organizations can manage employees and HR operations efficiently.

### Admin / HR Officer

Admin/HR users can:

* Manage employees
* View and update employee profiles
* View attendance records
* Manage attendance
* View leave requests
* Approve or reject leave requests
* Add approval comments
* View payroll information
* Update salary structures
* View reports and analytics
* Receive notifications

### Employee

Employees can:

* Register and log in
* View their dashboard
* View and manage permitted profile information
* Check in and check out
* View attendance history
* Apply for leave
* View leave request status
* View payroll information
* View documents
* Receive notifications

Employees have restricted access to their own information, while Admin/HR users have management and approval privileges.

---

# 🚀 Features

## 🔐 Authentication & Authorization

* Employee/HR registration
* Email and password login
* Password validation
* Secure password hashing
* JWT authentication
* Logout
* Email verification flow
* Role-based access control
* Protected routes
* Protected APIs

---

## 👤 Employee Management

Admin/HR can:

* Add employees
* View employees
* Search employees
* View employee profiles
* Edit employee details
* Deactivate employees

Employee profiles contain:

### Personal Details

* Full name
* Employee ID
* Email
* Phone
* Address
* Profile picture

### Job Details

* Department
* Position
* Joining date
* Employment status

### Salary Information

* Basic salary
* Allowances
* Deductions
* Net salary

### Documents

* Employee documents and related information

Employees can edit only permitted personal fields such as phone, address, and profile picture.

---

# 🕒 Attendance Management

Dayflow provides daily and weekly attendance tracking.

### Employee Features

* Check in
* Check out
* View today's attendance
* View attendance history
* View daily attendance
* View weekly attendance
* View working duration

### Attendance Status

* Present
* Absent
* Half-day
* Leave

### Business Rules

* An employee cannot check in multiple times on the same day.
* An employee cannot check out before checking in.
* An employee cannot check out multiple times.
* Employees can only view their own attendance.
* Admin/HR can view attendance of all employees.

---

# 🏖️ Leave & Time-Off Management

Employees can request time off.

### Leave Types

* Paid Leave
* Sick Leave
* Unpaid Leave

### Leave Request

Employees provide:

* Leave type
* Start date
* End date
* Remarks

### Leave Status

* Pending
* Approved
* Rejected

### Admin/HR

Admin/HR can:

* View all leave requests
* Approve requests
* Reject requests
* Add comments

Approved leave is reflected appropriately in employee records and attendance.

---

# 💰 Payroll & Salary Management

### Employee

Employees have read-only access to payroll information.

Displayed information includes:

* Employee
* Employee ID
* Basic salary
* Allowances
* Deductions
* Net salary
* Pay period

### Admin / HR

Admin/HR can:

* View payroll information
* Update salary structures
* Maintain payroll details

> Dayflow focuses on payroll visibility and management. It does not implement actual banking or payment processing.

---

# 🔔 Notifications

The system provides notifications for important HR events.

Notifications may be generated for:

* Leave submitted
* Leave approved
* Leave rejected
* Important HR updates
* Relevant attendance events

Notification features include:

* Read/unread status
* Mark as read
* Mark all as read
* Unread notification count
* Notification timestamps

---

# 📊 Reports & Analytics

Admin/HR users can access analytics and reports.

### Attendance Analytics

* Attendance trends
* Present percentage
* Absent percentage
* Leave percentage

### Leave Analytics

* Total requests
* Pending requests
* Approved requests
* Rejected requests
* Leave type distribution

### Payroll Analytics

* Salary overview
* Salary distribution
* Department salary overview

Charts are implemented using the frontend charting library.

---

# 🛠️ Technology Stack

## Frontend

* **Next.js**
* **React**
* **TypeScript**
* **Tailwind CSS**
* **shadcn/ui**
* **Lucide React**
* **Recharts**
* **React Hook Form**
* **Zod**

## Backend

* **Python**
* **FastAPI**
* **Pydantic**
* **SQLAlchemy**
* **Alembic**
* **JWT Authentication**

## Database

* **Neon PostgreSQL**

## Development

* Git
* GitHub
* REST APIs
* Swagger/OpenAPI through FastAPI

---

# 🏗️ System Architecture

```text
                    DAYFLOW HRMS
                         │
                         ▼
              ┌─────────────────────┐
              │    Next.js Frontend │
              │ React + TypeScript  │
              │ Tailwind + shadcn   │
              └──────────┬──────────┘
                         │
                      REST API
                         │
                         ▼
              ┌─────────────────────┐
              │   FastAPI Backend   │
              │ Python + Pydantic   │
              │ JWT + SQLAlchemy    │
              └──────────┬──────────┘
                         │
                         ▼
              ┌─────────────────────┐
              │  Neon PostgreSQL    │
              │    Database         │
              └─────────────────────┘
```

---

# 📁 Project Structure

```text
dayflow-hrms/
│
├── frontend/
│   ├── app/
│   ├── components/
│   ├── hooks/
│   ├── lib/
│   ├── services/
│   ├── types/
│   ├── public/
│   └── package.json
│
├── backend/
│   ├── app/
│   │   ├── main.py
│   │   ├── config.py
│   │   ├── database.py
│   │   ├── models/
│   │   ├── schemas/
│   │   ├── routers/
│   │   ├── services/
│   │   ├── auth/
│   │   └── utils/
│   ├── migrations/
│   └── requirements.txt
│
├── database/
│
├── tests/
│
├── docs/
│
├── .env.example
├── .gitignore
└── README.md
```

> The exact structure may evolve during development while maintaining separation between frontend, backend, database, and testing responsibilities.

---

# 🗄️ Database Design

Dayflow uses **Neon PostgreSQL** as the persistent database.

Core entities include:

```text
Users
  │
  ├── Roles
  │
  └── Employees
        │
        ├── Employee Profile
        ├── Attendance
        ├── Leave Requests
        ├── Payroll
        ├── Documents
        └── Notifications

Departments
Leave Types
Salary Components
Audit Logs
```

### Main Tables

* `users`
* `roles`
* `employees`
* `departments`
* `employee_profiles`
* `attendance`
* `leave_types`
* `leave_requests`
* `payroll`
* `salary_components`
* `documents`
* `notifications`
* `audit_logs`

SQLAlchemy is used for ORM-based database access and Alembic is used for database migrations.

---

# 🔌 API Overview

## Authentication

```text
POST /auth/signup
POST /auth/login
POST /auth/logout
POST /auth/verify-email
```

## Employees

```text
GET    /employees
GET    /employees/{id}
POST   /employees
PUT    /employees/{id}
DELETE /employees/{id}
```

## Profile

```text
GET /profile
PUT /profile
```

## Attendance

```text
GET  /attendance
POST /attendance/check-in
POST /attendance/check-out
GET  /attendance/{employee_id}
```

## Leave

```text
GET  /leave
POST /leave
GET  /leave/{id}
PUT  /leave/{id}/approve
PUT  /leave/{id}/reject
```

## Payroll

```text
GET /payroll
GET /payroll/{employee_id}
PUT /payroll/{employee_id}
```

## Notifications

```text
GET /notifications
PUT /notifications/{id}/read
PUT /notifications/read-all
```

## Analytics

```text
GET /analytics/attendance
GET /analytics/leave
GET /analytics/payroll
```

---

# 🔑 Environment Variables

Create a `.env` file locally.

Example:

```env
DATABASE_URL=your_neon_postgresql_connection_string
JWT_SECRET_KEY=your_secure_secret_key
CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000
ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRE_MINUTES=60
```

For GitHub, only commit:

```text
.env.example
```

Never commit:

```text
.env
```

---

# 💻 Installation

## 1. Clone the repository

```bash
git clone <YOUR_GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL>
cd dayflow-hrms
```

---

# 🎨 Frontend Setup

Navigate to the frontend:

```bash
cd frontend
```

Install dependencies:

```bash
npm install
```

Start development server:

```bash
npm run dev
```

The frontend will normally be available at:

```text
http://localhost:3000
```

Create a production build:

```bash
npm run build
```

Run linting if configured:

```bash
npm run lint
```

---

# ⚙️ Backend Setup

Navigate to the backend:

```bash
cd backend
```

Create a Python virtual environment:

```bash
python -m venv .venv
```

Activate it on Windows:

```bash
.venv\Scripts\activate
```

Activate it on Linux/macOS:

```bash
source .venv/bin/activate
```

Install dependencies:

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

Start FastAPI:

```bash
uvicorn app.main:app --reload
```

Backend will normally run at:

```text
http://localhost:8000
```

FastAPI API documentation:

```text
http://localhost:8000/docs
```

---

# 🐘 Neon PostgreSQL Setup

1. Create or open the Neon PostgreSQL project.
2. Copy the Neon connection string.
3. Add it to the local `.env` file:

```env
DATABASE_URL=your_neon_connection_string
```

4. Run the project's Alembic migrations.
5. Verify the database tables.
6. Load development seed data if configured.
7. Start the backend and verify that the API can communicate with Neon.

The Neon connection string must never be committed to GitHub.

---

# 🔄 Database Migration

From the backend directory:

```bash
alembic upgrade head
```

To create a migration after a model change:

```bash
alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe migration"
```

Then apply it:

```bash
alembic upgrade head
```

Only the designated database developer should normally create and maintain migrations in the team workflow.

---

# 👥 User Roles

## Admin / HR

Admin/HR has management and approval privileges.

Admin/HR can access:

* Dashboard
* Employees
* Attendance
* Leave Management
* Payroll
* Reports & Analytics
* Notifications
* Settings

## Employee

Employees have limited access to their own information.

Employees can access:

* Dashboard
* My Profile
* Attendance
* Leave Requests
* Payroll
* Documents
* Notifications
* Settings

---

# 🔒 Security

Dayflow implements security practices including:

* Password hashing
* JWT authentication
* Role-based authorization
* Protected frontend routes
* Protected backend endpoints
* Input validation
* ORM-based database access
* Environment variables
* CORS configuration
* No plaintext passwords
* No hard-coded database credentials

---

# 🧪 Testing

Important workflows to test include:

### Authentication

* Signup
* Login
* Invalid login
* Logout
* Email verification
* Role authorization

### Attendance

* Check-in
* Check-out
* Duplicate check-in prevention
* Invalid check-out
* Attendance visibility

### Leave

* Apply leave
* View leave
* Approve leave
* Reject leave
* Comments
* Employee access restrictions

### Payroll

* Employee read-only access
* Admin payroll updates

### Authorization

* Employee cannot access admin functionality
* Employee cannot access another employee's private information
* Employee cannot modify salary data

---

# 🌱 Demo Accounts

Development/demo accounts may include:

### Admin

```text
Email: admin@dayflow.com
```

### Employee

```text
Email: employee@dayflow.com
```

> Development passwords should be configured securely and should not be committed to the repository.

---

# 🤝 Team Development Workflow

Dayflow is developed by a 3-member team.

### Member 1

Frontend:

```text
frontend/
```

### Member 2

Backend:

```text
backend/
```

### Member 3

Database + Testing:

```text
database/
tests/
```

### Hourly Git Workflow

At the beginning of every hour:

```bash
git checkout main
git pull --rebase origin main
```

Each member works on their assigned module.

At the end of the hour:

```bash
git status
git diff
git add .
git commit -m "feat: describe completed work"
git push origin main
```

The members push sequentially so that every member's contribution reaches the shared `main` branch every hour.

### Important Git Rules

Never use:

```bash
git push --force
```

Never use destructive commands to overwrite another team member's work.

Always pull the latest `main` before continuing work.

---

# 📌 Development Priorities

The recommended development order is:

1. Project setup
2. Authentication
3. Role-based access
4. Employee management
5. Employee profiles
6. Attendance
7. Leave management
8. Leave approval
9. Payroll
10. Notifications
11. Reports and analytics
12. Integration testing
13. Bug fixing
14. Responsive and UI refinement

---

